IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `crm-time`
IMPORT `crm-offences`

-- Tests for crm-offences.l4. Every expected value is written from the text
-- of ss 4C, 4G, 4H, 4J and 4JA before the line was run; none is copied from
-- output.

§ `Tests of the offences module`


§§ `Section 4C: offences under 2 or more laws`

#ASSERT `s 4C(1) the offender is liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of those laws` `2 or more laws of the Commonwealth` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4C(1) the offender is liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of those laws` `2 or more laws of the Commonwealth` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4C(1) the offender is liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of those laws` `a law of the Commonwealth and the common law` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4C(1) the offender is liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of those laws` `a law of the Commonwealth and the common law` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4C(1) the offender is liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of those laws` `some other combination of laws` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4C(1) the offender is liable to be punished twice for the same act or omission` `2 or more laws of the Commonwealth` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4C(1) the offender is liable to be punished twice for the same act or omission` `a law of the Commonwealth and the common law` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4C(1) the offender is liable to be punished twice for the same act or omission` `some other combination of laws` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The arguments: an offence under a law of the Commonwealth; under a law of a State; under a law of a Territory; the offender has been punished under the State or Territory law.
#ASSERT `s 4C(2) the offender is liable to be punished for the offence under the law of the Commonwealth` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4C(2) the offender is liable to be punished for the offence under the law of the Commonwealth` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4C(2) the offender is liable to be punished for the offence under the law of the Commonwealth` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4C(2) the offender is liable to be punished for the offence under the law of the Commonwealth` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4C(2) the offender is liable to be punished for the offence under the law of the Commonwealth` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4C(2) the offender is liable to be punished for the offence under the law of the Commonwealth` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4C(3) the validity of that law is affected` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4C(3) the validity of that law is affected` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4C(3) the validity of that law is affected` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4C(3) the validity of that law is affected` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

